{"id":"s4.1.1","slug":"multiplying-three-digit-by-two-digit","title":"Multiplying Three-Digit Number by Two-Digit Number","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">To multiply a three-digit number ($abc$) by a two-digit number ($ef$), you can break it down into smaller, more manageable multiplications. Treat the three-digit number as two groups, $a$ and $bc$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\"><strong>Procedure:</strong></p><ol class=\"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li>Multiply the two-digit groups: $bc \\times ef$. The last two digits of this product form the end of your final answer. Note the carry.</li><li>Multiply the leading digit of the three-digit number by the two-digit number, and add the carry: $a \\times ef + \\text{carry}$. This result forms the beginning of your final answer.</li></ol><p>For example, $117 \\times 15$: First, $17 \\times 15 = 255$. The last two digits are 55, carry 2. Then, $1 \\times 15 + 2 = 17$. The result is 1755. This often involves other tricks for the intermediate steps.</p>","summary":"To multiply a three-digit number () by a two-digit number (), you can break it down into smaller, more manageable multiplications.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem multiplying a three-digit number by a two-digit number.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $314 \\times 17$.","answer":"5338","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $143 \\times 91$.","answer":"13013","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $202 \\times 34$.","answer":"6868","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $13 \\times 332$.","answer":"4316","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $202 \\times 53$.","answer":"10706","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $112 \\times 13$.","answer":"1456","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $221 \\times 23$.","answer":"5083","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $123 \\times 45$."